{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ad160e7a0e622e1c5ed69490c5a3356c77012902d8ce424ad65301850b4808e1","event_uuid":"4b388d01-2f17-4b55-b95a-79b08ea16f5c","position":{"commit_sha":"0eeb316d9edd58f6dae00696afa983167c4e30a6","position":"1787354963373951001-4b388d01-2f17-4b55-b95a-79b08ea16f5c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bf351e6f5f0f3a17d6f61c9dd0260bd2ca24a9845a182bb3e74269be25b79859","event_uuid":"9583747e-8319-45a2-92e9-95eb9b2b0649","position":{"commit_sha":"92a1670509d41a86cba22b65fcec68aa1143ea6e","position":"1787355838585483001-9583747e-8319-45a2-92e9-95eb9b2b0649"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f310668e828c33450498c74357401d6593679a7de5e6fe69b2701b26fa91d14a","event_uuid":"1f0b5400-d8a9-4a8e-be91-96a83ea7a9b2","position":{"commit_sha":"aa1ec549b2e19698e8984ccc935f41ab111b4974","position":"1787355844588337001-1f0b5400-d8a9-4a8e-be91-96a83ea7a9b2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Intent check (AC 1): introducing ticket b047-267f-3c3d-4374 records NO deliberate intent to keep check_comment_hygiene.py out of make lint. Its plan wired the detector as a named CI step in _build-and-test.yml following the scripts/check_*.py guard convention (modeled on check_verify_gate_parity.py) and never discusses the local lint target; the close comments cover acceptor fixes, not lint placement. Measured runtime (AC 1): 4.9s warm standalone on the full tree (macOS, repo .venv python); make lint baseline 17.8s -> ~22.7s with the gate. Decision on evidence: wire into make lint next to gen_env_registry.py --check, keeping the standalone CI step (mirrors the env-registry drift-gate precedent quoted in this ticket's observation).","timestamp":1787349470919659001}],"created_at":1787320331934232001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"21dba019-8ec0-4ab9-bbd4-e4634c885ac7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"84c7-486f-9a13-4c3f"},{"link_uuid":"4d1231bd-3838-47f4-ac25-aff5d383bc05","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"18eb-762c-3d15-4fdd"},{"link_uuid":"986727f8-a947-450a-80c3-869c26f077bd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e98e-5b38-c8e6-4ecc"},{"link_uuid":"cc12e00d-0175-461d-8411-64921813697c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"73b8-2d79-3046-44ce"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` is wired into CI as its own step (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`, \"comment-hygiene gate\") and is covered locally only by `tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py::test_the_real_tree_is_clean`, which runs in the **full** suite. It is **not** in `make lint`, so the local fast gate returns a clean verdict over trees CI rejects. Measured cost: bug 84c7 (change 1999) took a `Verified -1` for comment-hygiene findings `make lint` could not surface, wasting a full review cycle (two red jobs, the pytest one 15m09s with the hygiene guard as its only failure).\n\n## Approach\nEvidence gathered and recorded as a comment on this ticket resolves the ticket's option fork in favor of wiring the gate into `make lint`:\n- The introducing ticket `b047-267f-3c3d-4374` shows **no deliberate intent** to keep the gate out of `make lint` — its plan wired the detector as a named CI step per the `scripts/check_*.py` guard convention and never discusses the local lint target.\n- Measured runtime: ~4.9s warm on the full tree locally (`make lint` baseline 17.8s → ~22.7s). Acceptable next to the 15-minute CI cycle a miss costs, and squarely inside the documented env-var-drift-gate rationale already in the Makefile (\"running it here makes the local verdict agree with CI instead of surfacing staleness only in the full suite\").\n\nSo: add `python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` to the `lint` target next to `scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check`, mirroring that gate's precedent exactly — the standalone CI step in `_build-and-test.yml` **stays** (its if-present guard correctly handles patchsets predating the gate; the small double-run in CI matches the env-registry precedent). Add a wiring test in `tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py` (the gate's own test module) asserting the `lint` target body invokes the script, using the `_lint_target_body` idiom from `tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py`, plus a teeth case proving the assertion flips when the invocation is stripped from a synthetic Makefile copy.\n\n## Scope\n- `Makefile` — add the gate invocation (with a short rationale comment citing this ticket and the measured runtime) to the `lint` target.\n- `tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py` — baseline wiring assertion + removal-teeth test.\n\n## Testing\nRED first: the new wiring test fails against the unedited Makefile. GREEN: it passes once the lint-target line lands. Edge/teeth: stripping the invocation from a synthetic Makefile copy flips the assertion (proves it is not vacuous). `make lint` (now including the gate), `make typecheck`, and the targeted test module all pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The introducing ticket `b047-267f-3c3d-4374` is checked for deliberate intent to keep the gate out of `make lint`, and the finding (none found) plus the measured runtime (~4.9s standalone; lint 17.8s → ~22.7s) are recorded as a comment on this ticket.\n- [x] `make lint` runs `python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` in the `lint` target — verified by running `make lint` and by the new wiring test in `tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py`.\n- [x] The wiring test has teeth: a synthetic Makefile with the invocation stripped fails the same assertion, and this is itself a passing test at HEAD.\n- [x] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `pytest tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py` pass locally.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"Makefile","reason":"add python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py to the lint target with rationale comment"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py","reason":"baseline wiring assertion + removal-teeth test for the make lint wiring"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","18eb-762c-3d15-4fdd"],["relates_to","73b8-2d79-3046-44ce"],["relates_to","e98e-5b38-c8e6-4ecc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"9583747e-8319-45a2-92e9-95eb9b2b0649","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2d9a-78c5-5f87-4a22","ticket_type":"task","title":"comment-hygiene gate is reachable locally only via the full suite, not make lint","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d0d98d6f-1980-437f-aac1-ae0d34c8b8f1","3451ffeb-dced-4352-8e49-35361691fdff","6a003f35-0aca-41d5-b837-199fd8e1ee0c","672df6eb-a765-4207-affd-a5e96e802e4c","876c2929-f3e0-46f2-973c-0b9a11f0c32e","834515b4-09c8-416d-95d1-2ad9dcb4e6fd","4d1231bd-3838-47f4-ac25-aff5d383bc05","986727f8-a947-450a-80c3-869c26f077bd","cc12e00d-0175-461d-8411-64921813697c","4b388d01-2f17-4b55-b95a-79b08ea16f5c","9583747e-8319-45a2-92e9-95eb9b2b0649","1f0b5400-d8a9-4a8e-be91-96a83ea7a9b2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787361437333620001,"uuid":"b41e85fa-4560-4c6c-a9ef-c10e5e2b2389"}